{"name":"Madonna Blue","hex":"#71b5d1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"madonna","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Madonna.\nA representation of the Virgin Mary.\n\nA morally pure woman.\n\nA lady.","A representation of the Virgin Mary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A one-footed lien-to-tail trick, where the front foot is taken off and kicked out straight down behind the board."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/madonna"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Madonna","blocks":[{"text":"Madonna Louise Ciccone is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and actress. Dubbed the \"Queen of Pop\", she is known for her continual reinvention and versatility in music production, songwriting, and visual presentation. Her works, which concern social, political, sexual, and religious themes, have drawn acclaim and controversy. Regarded as one of the most influential musicians in history, Madonna broke gender barriers in popular music and has had a significant socio-cultural impact across her career."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/MadonnaO2171023_%2897_of_133%29_%2853269593787%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-MadonnaO2171023_%2897_of_133%29_%2853269593787%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna","wikidata":"Q1744"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/1280px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg/500px-Madonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_%281985%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Madonna performing in 1985 during the Virgin Tour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMadonna_-_Tampa_Bay_Times_(1985).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg/500px-Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Madonna_in_concert_wearing_fishnets_1987.jpg/500px-Madonna_in_concert_